    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3987" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλέκτωρ</span></b>  (A), [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰ],
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ορος</span>, ὁ</span>, poet. form of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλεκτρυών</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>cock</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕως ἐβόησεν ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Batr.
					192
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				12.14
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Simon.
				80
			</span></i> B, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				1671
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Eu.</u>
				861
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Herod.
				4.12
			</span></i>, etc.; later Prose, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				347
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PTeb.</u>
				140
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(i B. C.)</span><i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Pr.</u>
				24.66
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				30.31
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ev.Matt.</u>
				26.34
			</span></i>,al., <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				3.77
			</span></i>: metaph., of a trumpeter, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κοινὸς Ἀθηναίων ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Demad.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					4
				</span></i>
			; of a flute, Ion Trag.<i><span class="en">
				39
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλέκτορος λόφος</span>
			<i>yellow rattle, Rhinanthusmajor</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plin.
				<u>HN</u>
				27.40
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>husband, consort</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Tz.
			</span></i><i>ad Lyc.</i><i><span class="en">
				1094
			</span></i>, and so perh. in <i><span class="en">
				B.
				4.8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				851
			</span></i>. (Perh., 
				like
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκοίτης, ἄλοχος</span>
			, from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ-</span> copul., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λέκτρον</span>).</div>
